<title>UK: BTR share deals under microscope-paper.</title>
<headline>BTR share deals under microscope-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Trade and Industry is conducting a secret inquiry into trading of shares of industrial conglomerate BTR Plc, the Guardian newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>Department investigators believe a ring of up to a dozen well-known financial speculators benefited from advance knowledge that BTR was poised to take over its partly-owned Australian associate BTR Nylex Ltd  in the summer of last year, the Guardian said.</p>
<p>While both BTR and the department declined to comment, the inquiry is understood to have been launched under Section 177 of the Financial Services Act, which allows for department inspectors to be appointed when insider dealing laws are thought to have been breached, the Guardian said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
